      "kind": "intro",
      "page": 0,
      "text_preview": "A S THE DATA rate increases in high-speed serial wireline communications, transmission line losses and the resulting intersymbol interference (ISI) also increase. To compensate for the losses, transmitter (Tx) pre-emphasis ﬁlters and receiver (Rx) equalization can be used [1]. Recently, a variety of techniques that adaptively compensate for transmission line losses have been reported. In transmitt ..."
