      "title": "PARALLEL 12-CHANNEL TRANSCEIVER",
      "kind": "other",
      "page": 0,
      "text_preview": "The transceiver consists of a parallel 12-channel Tx, 12-channel Rx, and LC-VCO phase-locked loops (PLLs) (Fig. 1). In the transmitter circuit, incoming 32-bit parallel data is multiplexed to 5–6.4-Gb/s differential serial data. In contrast, in the receiver circuit, incoming 5–6.4-Gb/s differential serial data is demultiplexed to 32-bit parallel data. A quadrature LC-VCO oscillating at 2.5–3.2 GHz ..."
    },
    {
      "number": "III",
      "title": "CIRCUIT IMPLEMENTATION",
      "kind": "design",
      "page": 1,
      "text_preview": "A. Transmitter With Pre-Emphasis Filter The transmitter output stage consists of ﬁve blocks of differential drivers, forming a ﬁve-tap FIR ﬁlter (Fig. 5). The delay per tap is 1 UI, and a dedicated 8:1 MUX generates an appropriate delayed signal that drives each tap. We found that it was difﬁcult to achieve good linearity over the tap weights if the weights were controlled using independent curren ..."
