      "kind": "results",
      "page": 4,
      "text_preview": "Fig. 12 is a microphotograph of the 12-channel transceiver macro fabricated in 0.11m CMOS technology. The circular objects seen in the microphotograph are solder bumps for ﬂipchip bonding into a package. The transceiver consists of a parallel 12-channel Tx, a parallel 12-channel Rx, and PLLs. The characteristics of the design and performance measurement are shown in Table I. The transmitter and re ..."
    },
    {
      "number": "V",
      "title": "CONCLUSION",
      "kind": "conclusion",
      "page": 6,
      "text_preview": "We implemented a 5–6.4-Gb/s 12-channel high-speed transm CMOS technology. To reduce the skew ceiver using 0.11between channels, we used a skew-compensated clock, resulting in less than 0.08-UI skew between channels. To compensate for transmission-line losses, we implemented a ﬁve-tap Tx pre-emphasis ﬁlter and an Rx second-order equalizer, each of which compensate for losses of up to 20 dB. We also ..."
